Z||000000||Rex||04-13-2001||10:07 PM||||The " Manual " says the fan comes on at 240 degrees or when the A/C is operating. Does anyone think this is too late to activate? If so are there any remedies? Thanks in advance for input.<BR>86 Red SE V-6||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||04-13-2001||10:27 PM||||Rodney Dickman has just made available replacement fan switches that come on at about 210 and cut off at 195 (I think these are the right values).  This way you keep the regular thermostat and the ECM operates in the temp range it was designed for.  This sounds like a good idea to me.<P>See Rodney's web site at <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
